This will generate a random code in the format of `xxxxxxxx-xxxx-4xxx-yxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx`. You can use this code in your application and store it in a database or display it to the user.
4. Call the `generateRandomCode()` function wherever you need the code to be generated:
```typescript
import { Component } from '@angular/core';
import { UUID } from 'uuid';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-root',
  template: `
    <button (click)="generateRandomCode()">Generate Code</button>
  `
})
export class AppComponent {
  generateRandomCode();
}
```
